      *****************************************************************
      *     FRONT-END SUBROUTINE FOR PO INQUIRY
      *****************************************************************


      *****************************************************************
      **          M O D I F I C A T I O N    H I S T O R Y
      *****************************************************************
      *C FEBRUARY 23, 1993  CR KALMAN    NO REQ #
      *C CLEARED OUT THE BASE-STHIST-OPEN-INDIC TO FORCE
      *C THE HISTORY DPORECD FILE TO OPEN IN THIS SUBROUTINE.
      *C PREVIOUSLY THE INDICATOR WAS BEING PASSED WITH A VALUE
      *C GREATER THAN SPACES CAUSING THIS SUBRTN TO THINK THE
      *C FILE WAS OPEN. THIS WOULD CAUSE THE USER TO GET A MCH3601.
      *C THIS CHANGE IS ONLY A BAND-AID. THE LOGIC TO OPEN THE FILES
      *C SHOULD REALLY BE CHANGED.
      *C
      *C 02/21/94   JEFF BUNGO   REQUEST #6449
      *C    ADDED NEW FIELDS TO THE HISTORY DATABASES TO MATCH THE
      *C    LIVE DATABASES.  CHANGED/RECOMPILED THIS PROGRAM TO
      *C    USE THE NEW HISTORY FIELDS.
      *C
      *C 06/10/96   JEFF BUNGO
      *C    EXPAND DATE FIELDS FOR YEAR 2000 COMPLIANCE.
      *C    RECOMPILE TO PICK UP NEW FILE FORMATS.
      *C
      *C 02/06/97   JEFF BUNGO
      *C    ON F2 FOR MULTI PLANT DATABASES DO OVERRIDES TO
      *C    SWITCH DATABASES.  ALSO MOVE THE OPENS OF THE FILES
      *C    USED IN THIS PROGRAM TO AFTER THE OVERRIDES.
      *C
      *C 03/25/98   CA YODER
      *C    PROGRAM WAS BLOWING UP IN AKRON WHEN TRYING TO
      *C    FIND PO IN MULTIPLE LIBRARIES.  CHANGED COMMAND-LEN
      *C    DEFINITION, AND CHANGED WHEN THE PO KEY IS MOVED TO
      *C    THE INPUT RECORD UNTIL AFTER THE FILE IS OPEN.
      *C
      *C 06/18/99   JE COFFMAN
      *C    ADDED LOGIC AT DANVILLE'S REQUEST TO ALLOW USERS
      *C    TO VIEW A DUPLICATE PURCHASE ORDER IN THE HISTORY
      *C    DATABASE. THE USER WILL NEED TO RETRIEVE THE 1ST
      *C    ENTRY IF IT IS NOT THE LATEST BY DATE VIA THE PU8
      *C    FUNCTION AND THEN THEY SHOULD BE ABLE TO INQUIRE
      *C    AGAINST THE DUPLICATE PO IN THE HISTORY DATABASE.
      *C---------------------------------------------------------------
DCR01 *C MAR 10, 2005  DCR01  DAN RAUCH       REQUEST# 2005-78515
DCR01 *C    DISPLAY FILE PROCESSING CHANGED FROM USING ZCSISINQ
DCR01 *C    NEW DISPLAY FILE ZSPOINQ CREATED - FORMATS COPIED
DCR01 *C    FROM ZCSISINQ.
DCR01 *****************************************************************
008700
